+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
+ *
+ * K60 audio core skeleton: ADSP/PAS1 + AudioReach GPR plumbing.
+ *
+ * EXPERIMENTAL: this is a compileable skeleton, not a working audio driver.
+ * It ports the structure of PongPower/PongAudio.cpp and the pure packet
+ * builders of PongPower/ShengAudioReach.c (both BSD-2-Clause-Patent), with
+ * K60 board constants from the live FDT.
+ *
+ * K60 facts used here (see /mnt/e/k60-work/scratch/audio-work/EVIDENCE.md):
+ *   - ADSP: remoteproc-adsp@03000000, qcom,cape-adsp-pas,
+ *     reserved memory 0x9fd00000 + 0x3100000 (49 MiB)
+ *   - SMEM: 0x80900000 + 0x200000; IPCC: 0xed18000 IRQ 261;
+ *     GPR: qcom,gpr reg=2, qcom,glink-channels="adsp_apps",
+ *     qcom,intents=<0x200 0x14>
+ *   - AudioReach PCM: 48 kHz, stereo, 32-bit, 480-frame periods,
+ *     8 slots in a 64 KiB low-DMA lease, SID 0x1801
+ *   - TDM: tert MI2S/TDM, 1.536 MHz, tx-lines=0x3 (SD0+SD1),
+ *     GPIO121=SCK/123=WS/122=SD0/124=SD1
+ *
+ * Eight-step pipeline status (E:/k60-work/docs/PORTING-PIPELINE.md):
+ *   (1) same-hardware: Pong/Sheng AudioReach implementations (REUSE.md)
+ *   (2) official docs: no K60 audio datasheet; AudioReach opcodes from
+ *       Sheng/Pong source
+ *   (3) reverse + device data: K60 live FDT only; no ADSP firmware dump
+ *   (4) wide validation: K60 FDT + liuqin ADSP carveout match (EVIDENCE.md)
+ *   (5) plan: PLAN.md P4
+ *   (6) deep dive: REPORT.md
+ *   (7) verification: compile-only; ADSP/PAS1 execution TODO
+ *   (8) on-device: not attempted
+ */
